WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.450
There are two clocks here.

2
00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:04.950
Directory work fails at cutover,
where someone is watching.

3
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:09.675
Certificate work fails at expiry,
months later and far from its cause.

4
00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:12.485
So a program that measures
progress by cutover

5
00:00:12.485 --> 00:00:15.150
dates reports success
right up to the outage.

6
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.250
And the cloud options only
cover part of the estate.

7
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:23.266
Cloud PKI issues only to Intune-managed
devices, which don't include servers,

8
00:00:23.266 --> 00:00:27.725
and domain controllers need
certificates for as long as they exist.

9
00:00:27.725 --> 00:00:32.736
The decision for the sponsor and the CIO:
run the move off the old certificate

10
00:00:32.736 --> 00:00:37.588
authority as its own program, with its
own owner, sequenced by expiry dates.

11
00:00:37.588 --> 00:00:39.890
And those dates are
getting closer together.
